{"created": "2026-07-27T14:50:32.273728+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-27T14:50:33.108588+00:00", "id": 19857425, "conceptrecid": "19857424", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19857425", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.19857424", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19857425", "metadata": {"title": "Marine Engine Fault", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.19857425", "publication_date": "2026-04-28", "description": "<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">This record contains an experimental dataset for condition monitoring, fault diagnosis, and anomaly detection on a marine diesel engine. All data were acquired on a <strong>Matsui Iron Works MU323DGSC</strong> engine under controlled test-bench conditions. The dataset comprises a baseline reference-performance recording together with five induced fault/anomaly classes, each recorded at one or more fixed engine loads, providing labelled time-series suitable for developing and benchmarking data-driven diagnostic and anomaly-detection methods.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">The five fault scenarios are:</p>\n<ul class=\"[li_&amp;]:mb-0 [li_&amp;]:mt-1 [li_&amp;]:gap-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:pb-1 list-disc flex flex-col gap-1 pl-8 mb-3\">\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\"><strong>Compressor air-filter clogging</strong> &mdash; 40, 60, 75, 85 % load</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\"><strong>Air-cooler fouling</strong> &mdash; 40, 60, 75, 85 % load</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\"><strong>Injection-valve nozzle clogging</strong> &mdash; a one-hole restricted nozzle (40 / 60 / 85 % load) and a more severe two-hole restricted nozzle under a load program</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\"><strong>Cooling-water pump cavitation</strong> &mdash; 60, 85 % load</li>\n<li class=\"font-claude-response-body whitespace-normal break-words pl-2\"><strong>Turbine degradation</strong> &mdash; 40, 60, 85 % load</li>\n</ul>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\">Each scenario was produced by physically inducing the corresponding abnormal condition on the engine; the procedure for each is described in the README.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>Data records.</strong> The dataset contains 16 CSV files &mdash; one baseline reference file and 15 fault-scenario files &mdash; totalling roughly 115,000 time-stamped samples across about 70 measured and derived channels (engine speed, in-cylinder pressures, exhaust and cooling-circuit temperatures, flows, pressures, and work/efficiency quantities). All files are UTF-8 encoded and use a consistent three-row header (full variable name, shorthand symbol, unit). The scenario files share a single 73-column schema whose first three columns are <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Time_abs</code>, <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Time_rel</code>, and a binary <code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">Anomaly State</code> label (0 = pre-anomaly, 1 = anomaly); the two injection-nozzle files contain anomalous operation only. The reference file uses a separate 70-column baseline schema (no anomaly label). Two channels (Compressor Filter Loss and Turbine Back Pressure) were not recorded in five runs and are left empty in those files. A file-level index (<code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">dataset_index</code>) and a variable dictionary (<code class=\"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]\">variable_dictionary</code>) documenting every channel, its unit, data type, and per-file presence are included, along with the script used to normalise the raw exports.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>Associated publication.</strong> This dataset accompanies the Data Descriptor \"[manuscript title]\" ([author list]), submitted to <em>Scientific Data</em>; a preprint is available at arXiv:[ID]. Please cite both the Data Descriptor and this dataset when using the data.</p>\n<p class=\"font-claude-response-body break-words whitespace-normal\"><strong>License.</strong> Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "BahooToroody, Ahmad", "affiliation": "Aalto University", "orcid": "0000-0002-7126-4244"}, {"name": "Bondarenko, Oleksiy", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0002-1811-2372"}, {"name": "Abaei, Mohammad Mahdi", "affiliation": "University of Turku", "orcid": "0000-0003-1480-2007"}, {"name": "Niki, Yoichi", "affiliation": null, "orcid": "0000-0001-6294-542X"}, {"name": "Zio, Enrico", "affiliation": "Politecnico di Milano", "orcid": "0000-0002-7108-637X"}], "keywords": ["marine diesel engine", "maritime machinery", "predictive maintenance", "Prognostics and Health Management", "condition monitoring", "fault diagnosis", "anomaly detection", "degradation modeling", "time-series data", "engine fault dataset"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.48550/arXiv.2607.19444", "relation": "isDescribedBy", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "dates": [{"type": "issued", "description": "Public release of Version 1.0 on Zenodo"}], "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "grants": [{"code": "362947", "internal_id": "10.13039/501100002341::362947", "funder": {"name": "Research Council of Finland", "doi": "10.13039/501100002341", "acronym": "AKA"}, "title": "New Transition Model from Offline Predictive Maintenance to Real-Time (TRANSITION \u2013 MODEL)"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "19857424"}}]}}, "title": "Marine Engine Fault", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19857425", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19857425?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19857425", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19857425", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19857425", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857424", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19857424", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19857424", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.19857424", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19857425/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:19857425/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/media-files", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/versions/latest", "latest_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/19857425/latest", "versions": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/versions", "draft": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/draft", "access_links": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/access/links", "access_grants": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/access/grants", "access_users": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/access/users", "access_request": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/access/request", "access": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/19857425/access", "communities": "https://zen